<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<speak version="1.0" xml:lang="en-GB">
  <!-- AI CUE: TITLE: clear and composed; give the heading room. Do not perform as narrative prose. -->
  <p><s>Chapter 44: The General's Silence</s></p><break time="700ms"/>
  <break time="1400ms"/>
  <!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>For six days after the crossing Aurveth hardly spoke.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: TENSION: use controlled, attentive phrasing and let pauses preserve suspense. Do not become theatrical. -->
  <p>She lay at the back of the cave at Crow Scar, against the wall, with her great head on the stone and her one eye open, looking at nothing. She ate when Lisska brought her meat, a little. She drank from the spring that came out of the rock. She didn't go out. When Calder came up through the frozen Fellwood at night and climbed the crag and sat down beside her, she let him put his hand on her brow, and kept her silence.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: TENSION: use controlled, attentive phrasing and let pauses preserve suspense. Do not become theatrical. -->
  <p>He could feel her through the bronze mark. Something going on in her, all the time, day and night, like a millwheel turning under the floor of a mill. Slow and huge and never stopping.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: QUESTION: shape the sentence as a genuine question, following its context; avoid an exaggerated upward lilt. -->
  <p>Is she ill? said Lisska, on the third night. She doesn't feel ill. She feels like she's listening.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: DIALOGUE: speak naturally; distinguish the speaker subtly using the wording and context. Do not invent an accent or emotion. -->
  <p>"I don't know, little one."</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>Ask her.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: DIALOGUE: speak naturally; distinguish the speaker subtly using the wording and context. Do not invent an accent or emotion. -->
  <p>"I have."</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>Ask her again.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>He did. He sat beside Aurveth's head in the dark of the cave and asked her what was wrong.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: REFLECTION: use measured, inward phrasing; keep emotion restrained and grounded in the text. -->
  <p>She didn't answer for so long that he thought she wasn't going to. Then, without moving her head:</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>Not yet, she said.</p>
 <break time="1400ms"/>
  <!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>On the seventh night, midwinter night, she lifted her head.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>He'd come up late. It was bitter cold, the coldest night yet, so cold the air hurt to breathe and the snow squeaked under his boots like something alive. The moon was full and very high and white, and the Fellwood lay under it black and silver, and from the ledge at the mouth of the cave you could see the whole of the Marches spread out below in the moonlight: the forest, the hills, the white snake of the river, the island, Greyhold's long wall far down on the other bank with every window lit, white and steady, as only Hearthmere's lamps burned.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: DIALOGUE: speak naturally; distinguish the speaker subtly using the wording and context. Do not invent an accent or emotion. -->
  <p>"They're keeping midwinter," he said. He'd sat down by the fire Lisska had lit for him in the mouth of the cave, and was holding his hands out to it. "Greyhold. Every light's on."</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>Aurveth lifted her head off the stone.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: TENSION: use controlled, attentive phrasing and let pauses preserve suspense. Do not become theatrical. -->
  <p>He felt the slow turning in her catch, at last, and become something else.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>I want to go down, she said.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>He looked at her.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: QUESTION: shape the sentence as a genuine question, following its context; avoid an exaggerated upward lilt. -->
  <p>Not to the island. I will not set foot on that island. Not yet. She was getting up onto her feet, her scarred back stiff in the cold. Near it. On the river. Where I can feel. She turned her head and looked at him with her one eye. Will you come with me? I would rather not go alone.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: REFLECTION: use measured, inward phrasing; keep emotion restrained and grounded in the text. -->
  <p>Can we come? said Lisska at once.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>No, child. You and Kharrak will stay on the hill above his farm and watch. If anything moves on the far bank, a boat, a torch, anything, you will call him.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: QUESTION: shape the sentence as a genuine question, following its context; avoid an exaggerated upward lilt. -->
  <p>What are you going to feel? said Kharrak, from the cave mouth. What's there?</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>Aurveth didn't answer him either.</p>
 <break time="1400ms"/>
  <!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>She went down off the ledge an hour before midnight, with Calder flat on her neck behind her head and his arms round the ridge between the plates.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>She went low. Lower than he'd ever flown with her. She came off the crag and dropped straight down to the Fellwood and went along over the top of it so low that her belly brushed the snow off the highest branches, and the trees went by under him in the dark, silver and black, a hand's breadth below. He could hear the snow falling off them behind her in long soft rushes. She went west along the top of the forest, low and silent, with her great wings barely moving, like an owl along a hedge.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>Over the shoulder of the hill. Over his own top field, white, with the black ring of the burned stubble under the snow. Down past the Fenn farm, dark and empty. Out over the edge of the land, and down, onto the river.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>She landed on the ice a league above the island, under the Saltreach bank.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: ACTION: make the phrasing alert and precise; only raise pace or intensity slightly when the sentence supports it. Keep every word clear. -->
  <p>He'd never have found the place. She'd picked it from the air. A long reach of the river where the bank came down steep and high on the east side, with a hanging wood on top of it, so that the bank threw a deep black shadow out across the ice under the high moon. No tower on the Hearthmere side could see into it. No window at Greyhold. They came down out of the dark into the shadow with her wings spread wide, and her great feet touched the snow on the ice, and then her weight, and the ice groaned, a long deep sound that went away across the river and came back.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>And held.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>She lowered her neck, and he slid down off it onto the ice.</p>
 <break time="1400ms"/>
  <!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>He'd stood on the river before, crossing to the island. It was different, standing on it beside her. She was so heavy. He could feel the ice bearing her through the soles of his boots. Every time she shifted, a small deep creak went away from her across the river in all directions, like rings going out across a pond.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>The island lay downriver, a league off, a long dark shape in the white with the stump of its tower against the sky. She didn't look at it. She looked down. At the ice under her feet.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>She lay down flat. All of her. Her belly on the ice, her great wings spread out on either side of her across the snow like two dark sails laid down to dry, her tail out straight behind. She stretched her long neck out along the ice in front of her, and laid her jaw on it, and then turned her head a little, and pressed her throat down against the ice, as a man lies down in a field with his ear to the ground to hear if horses are coming.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>She lay like that.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: TENSION: use controlled, attentive phrasing and let pauses preserve suspense. Do not become theatrical. -->
  <p>He stood beside her in the black shadow under the bank and waited.</p>
 <break time="1400ms"/>
  <!-- AI CUE: TENSION: use controlled, attentive phrasing and let pauses preserve suspense. Do not become theatrical. -->
  <p>It came up into her slowly.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>He felt what it did to her, if not all of what she felt. Through the bronze mark, faint at first, and then stronger, like cold coming up into your feet from the ground when you stand too long.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>Something below.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>Below the ice. Below the river. Below the riverbed, and the gravel and the clay under that, and the rock under that. Further down than anything he could think about. He felt her reach down into it, through her throat pressed against the ice. And he felt her touch it.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>Vast.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>It came up through the mark into him, and it was so big that he put his hand out and leaned on her flank to stay standing. Bigger than her. Bigger than the island. Bigger than Coldtarn, bigger than the Scarfell, so big that his head gave up trying to hold the size of it. Lying down there. Under everything. Awake, as surely as the lion on the path under the oaks had been awake, and turning over and over in a bed it couldn't get out of.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>And bound.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: ACTION: make the phrasing alert and precise; only raise pace or intensity slightly when the sentence supports it. Keep every word clear. -->
  <p>He didn't have a word for it. He felt it through her like a rope too tight round a beast's leg, when you put your hand on the beast: the pressure, the place where something is held that shouldn't be held. Bound, down there in the dark, with something round it, and the something had been there so long that the thing it held had grown round it, like a tree round a nail.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: ACTION: make the phrasing alert and precise; only raise pace or intensity slightly when the sentence supports it. Keep every word clear. -->
  <p>Under all of that there was something worse. It came up through the bronze mark into him for one moment, the last thing, the deepest, and it was like nothing he'd ever felt from any beast or any man. It was like a bone set badly. A leg broken and healed crooked, that walks, and carries weight, and is wrong all the way through, every step it takes.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>He took his hand off her flank and stood on the ice and was sick.</p>
 <break time="1400ms"/>
  <!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>When he could stand again she hadn't moved.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>She lay flat on the ice with her throat pressed down and her wings spread, and her one eye was open and staring at nothing. What he felt in her was what he'd felt on the hill above the Fenn farm, when she smelled the lion on his coat and put her head down in the snow. The old thing, turning over, very deep. Only now it had stopped turning, and was awake in her.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: DIALOGUE: speak naturally; distinguish the speaker subtly using the wording and context. Do not invent an accent or emotion. -->
  <p>"Aurveth," he said.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>Nothing.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: DIALOGUE: speak naturally; distinguish the speaker subtly using the wording and context. Do not invent an accent or emotion. -->
  <p>"Aurveth. What is it? What's down there?"</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>He felt the question go into her, down through the mark, and land. He felt her close round it, like a hand closing over something small so nobody can see it.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>Do not ask me, she said.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: TENSION: use controlled, attentive phrasing and let pauses preserve suspense. Do not become theatrical. -->
  <p>Her voice was very quiet, like his mother's when she was very angry or very frightened and didn't want him to know which.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>Not yet. I will tell you when I can bear to.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>It went into him and stuck, like a burr in wool.</p>
 <break time="1400ms"/>
  <!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>They stayed on the ice for most of the night.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: ACTION: make the phrasing alert and precise; only raise pace or intensity slightly when the sentence supports it. Keep every word clear. -->
  <p>She didn't get up. He sat down in the snow beside her head, against the curve of her jaw, where it was warm, and pulled his coat round him and waited. He didn't ask again. He put his hand on her jaw and left it there.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: TENSION: use controlled, attentive phrasing and let pauses preserve suspense. Do not become theatrical. -->
  <p>On the hill above the Fenn farm, a league and a half away, he could feel the other two. Watching. Close enough to talk.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: QUESTION: shape the sentence as a genuine question, following its context; avoid an exaggerated upward lilt. -->
  <p>What's she doing? said Lisska. Whispering, as if they might hear her at Greyhold. She feels so heavy. Like she's carrying something. Is she?</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: DIALOGUE: speak naturally; distinguish the speaker subtly using the wording and context. Do not invent an accent or emotion. -->
  <p>"I think so."</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: QUESTION: shape the sentence as a genuine question, following its context; avoid an exaggerated upward lilt. -->
  <p>What did she find?</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: DIALOGUE: speak naturally; distinguish the speaker subtly using the wording and context. Do not invent an accent or emotion. -->
  <p>"She won't say."</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>Then I'll go and dig it up, said Kharrak.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>He said it calmly. That was what made Calder's head come up: no red tide at all. Whatever's down there. Under the island. I can dig. I'll dig down through the island and see what it is, and then she won't have to say.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>Aurveth lifted her head off the ice.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>It was the first time she'd moved in an hour. She turned it on her long neck and looked up through the dark toward the hill where Kharrak lay, a league and a half off, as if she could see him.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>If you put one claw into that island, she said, very quietly, I will break your wing myself. The good one. And I will hold you down while it heals crooked.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>The hill went silent.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>He felt Kharrak hear it, and go still, and stay still. He felt Lisska go small and flat in the snow beside Kharrak.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>Aurveth laid her head back down on the ice.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>I am sorry, she said, after a while. To all of them. I have never been frightened like this. Not when Ragnald died. Not when Sigrun died. Not when the field was burning and I was going out from the edges in. Leave it alone. All of you. Please. Until I understand it.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>Nobody answered her.</p>
 <break time="1400ms"/>
  <!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>At midnight the singing came across the ice.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: ACTION: make the phrasing alert and precise; only raise pace or intensity slightly when the sentence supports it. Keep every word clear. -->
  <p>He heard it first as nothing. A change in the air. Then a sound, so faint he thought it was the blood in his ears, or the wind in the hanging wood on the bank above. A long low sound, rising and falling. Coming from downriver, from beyond the island, where Greyhold's long wall stood on the Hearthmere bank with every window lit.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>Voices. Hundreds of them. Singing.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>He'd never heard anything carry so far. Four leagues and more, across the frozen river, on the still bitter air, with no wind and no water moving to stop it. It came to him thin and very clear, like a voice heard across a valley in the early morning.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>They're singing, said Lisska, on the hill. The knights. On the wall. All of them. It's the same words over and over.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: DIALOGUE: speak naturally; distinguish the speaker subtly using the wording and context. Do not invent an accent or emotion. -->
  <p>"I can't make out the words."</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: TENSION: use controlled, attentive phrasing and let pauses preserve suspense. Do not become theatrical. -->
  <p>I can. My ears are better than yours. She was quiet a moment, listening. She said them to him one at a time, in her small bright voice, keeping time with the far singing:</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>Keep. The watch. Below.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>And do not ask.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>Beside him on the ice, Aurveth shuddered.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: ACTION: make the phrasing alert and precise; only raise pace or intensity slightly when the sentence supports it. Keep every word clear. -->
  <p>It went through her from the tip of her nose to the end of her tail. The ice under her groaned with it, a long deep sound going out across the river in rings. Her wings, spread out on the snow, pulled in against her sides all at once, like a bird's when a hawk goes over.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: REFLECTION: use measured, inward phrasing; keep emotion restrained and grounded in the text. -->
  <p>He sat in the snow beside her with his hand on her jaw and the singing coming across the ice. He thought of the carving over the arch, that Lisska could see and Aurveth could read, and wouldn't. He thought of his mother at Bel's table, with her face gone the colour of ash. Don't ask me again, Calder.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>The singing stopped.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: TENSION: use controlled, attentive phrasing and let pauses preserve suspense. Do not become theatrical. -->
  <p>It stopped all at once, as if a door had shut. The huge frozen silence of the river came back across the ice.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>Aurveth didn't lift her head again until the sky went grey in the east.</p>
 <break time="1400ms"/>
  <!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>When she did, she got up off the ice without a word, stiffly, the frost cracking off her scales. She lowered her neck for him. He climbed up behind her head and found the ridge and held on, and she went up off the river into the dawn, low, along the top of the white Fellwood.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>She didn't go to the Scar. She put him down in the snow at the top of Bel's hollow, at the edge of the trees, and when he'd slid off she went on east alone, low over the forest, and didn't look back.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>He stood in the snow and felt the other two coming home behind her.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: QUESTION: shape the sentence as a genuine question, following its context; avoid an exaggerated upward lilt. -->
  <p>What do we tell them? said Lisska. Your mother. Bel. When they ask where you went.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>He looked down the hollow at the house. Smoke from the chimney, going straight up. Ada would be up. She was always up.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: DIALOGUE: speak naturally; distinguish the speaker subtly using the wording and context. Do not invent an accent or emotion. -->
  <p>"Nothing," he said.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: QUESTION: shape the sentence as a genuine question, following its context; avoid an exaggerated upward lilt. -->
  <p>Nothing?</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: DIALOGUE: speak naturally; distinguish the speaker subtly using the wording and context. Do not invent an accent or emotion. -->
  <p>"Nothing about tonight. Not to Ma. Not to Bel, or Fisk, or Wren. Not to anybody." It came out steadier than he'd thought it would. "And nobody goes near that island. Not a claw on it. Not till she says."</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: TENSION: use controlled, attentive phrasing and let pauses preserve suspense. Do not become theatrical. -->
  <p>The forest was quiet. Then Kharrak, far off, low.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>I heard her, said Kharrak. I heard you. A pause. I won't.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: NARRATION: relaxed, clear, and conversational; preserve sentence rhythm and avoid a dramatic announcer style. -->
  <p>He went down the hollow and in at the kitchen door.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: ACTION: make the phrasing alert and precise; only raise pace or intensity slightly when the sentence supports it. Keep every word clear. -->
  <p>Ada was at the hearth with her hand on the warm stone, saying the hearth-words over the banked fire. She finished them before she looked round. She always did. Then she looked at him: at the frost in his hair, and the sick down the front of his coat, and his face.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: DIALOGUE: speak naturally; distinguish the speaker subtly using the wording and context. Do not invent an accent or emotion. -->
  <p>"You've been out all night," she said.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: DIALOGUE: speak naturally; distinguish the speaker subtly using the wording and context. Do not invent an accent or emotion. -->
  <p>"Yes."</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: DIALOGUE: speak naturally; distinguish the speaker subtly using the wording and context. Do not invent an accent or emotion. -->
  <p>"Where?"</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: DIALOGUE: speak naturally; distinguish the speaker subtly using the wording and context. Do not invent an accent or emotion. -->
  <p>"On the river."</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: DIALOGUE: speak naturally; distinguish the speaker subtly using the wording and context. Do not invent an accent or emotion. -->
  <p>"And what's on the river?"</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: REFLECTION: use measured, inward phrasing; keep emotion restrained and grounded in the text. -->
  <p>He thought of it. Lying down there under everything, awake, bound, wrong like a bone set badly.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: DIALOGUE: speak naturally; distinguish the speaker subtly using the wording and context. Do not invent an accent or emotion. -->
  <p>"Ice," he said.</p>
  <break time="450ms"/><!-- AI CUE: ACTION: make the phrasing alert and precise; only raise pace or intensity slightly when the sentence supports it. Keep every word clear. -->
  <p>His mother looked at him for a long moment. Then she turned back to the fire and put another log on it, and didn't ask again.</p>
<break time="450ms"/></speak>
